5. ECOG score ≤ 1;
6. The expected survival time is ≥ 3 months;
7. During the screening period, the assessments showed adequate organ and bone marrow function,
8. Echocardiography shows left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≥50%; no arrhythmias requiring treatment; QT interval corrected by the Fridericia method (QTcF) ≤470 ms; baseline blood oxygen saturation \>91% in ambient air conditions;
9. Prior to tumor sampling, adverse reactions induced by previous treatments have recovered to Grade 1 (5.0) or below according to the Common Terminology Criteria for Adverse Events (CTCAE) version 5.0;
10. From the signing of the informed consent form to one year after TIL cell infusion, agree to adopt effective non-pharmacological contraception measures;
